Now I see the key code. Let me look at the `get(basic_string_view<Char> name)` function:

```cpp
template <typename Char> format_arg get(basic_string_view<Char> name) const {
    if (!has_named_args()) return {};
    const auto& named_args =
        (is_packed() ? values_[-1] : args_[-1].value_).named_args;
    for (size_t i = 0; i < named_args.size; ++i) {
      if (named_args.data[i].name == name) return get(named_args.data[i].id);
    }
    return {};
  }
```

The `values_[-1]` accesses index -1 of the values array. This is the stack-buffer-underflow! When `is_packed()` is true, it reads `values_[-1]`. The `values_` array is a stack array in `arg_data`. Let me look at the `arg_data` structure.

